    {"dot": "cyan", "title": "One conversation can advertise two products", "items": ["HTTP UserAgent claims belong to the client IP. Server-derived claims use the server endpoint; a response-only HTTP record uses its source IP as the server (software.go:364-379).", "A service-signature product belongs to the observed service IP, with ObservationRole=server (service_probe.go:88-94).", "Ordinary client/server observations are also persisted as Software records. The right column highlights their optional enrichment, not a separate destination replacing audit output (software.go:109-157,721-743)."]},
    {"dot": "amber", "title": "Webtech is a deliberately weaker claim", "items": ["Passive WebTech emits webtech_advertisement, low confidence and origin role, without asserting an ObservedHost (webtech.go:142-149).", "The Software path explicitly skips CVE and exploit enrichment for Passive WebTech. That claim cannot silently become a vulnerable-host finding (software.go:725-734).", "Banners, User-Agents and web advertisements can be misleading. Verify the installed package and configuration before concluding exposure (docs/deep-packet-inspection.md:50; docs/vulnerability-analysis.md:36-46)."]},
